WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.380
They both say bitcoin. Isn't it the same trade?

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:12.578
Plain spot, with no borrowing, swaps one asset for another.

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:18.557
The linear perpetual we cover here is a contract position that settles profit and loss as the price moves.

00:00:18.557 --> 00:00:20.870
It's not buying bitcoin you can withdraw.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.932
Going long usually means hoping the price rises.

00:00:34.932 --> 00:00:37.279
Going short usually means hoping it falls.

00:00:37.279 --> 00:00:39.905
Get the direction wrong, and either side loses.

00:00:39.905 --> 00:00:43.090
Being able to short doesn't make it easier to make money.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.080
Should I level up from spot to futures?

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:06.769
No need. Futures are a different risk structure, not a level you must reach.

00:01:06.769 --> 00:01:10.060
You can understand them and still choose not to use them.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:28.127
Plain spot without borrowing has no margin liquidation like futures do.

00:01:28.127 --> 00:01:30.530
But the asset can still lose a lot of value.

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:33.370
No liquidation doesn't mean your money is protected.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:43.600
No.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.780
Know what you're trading first. Then study leverage.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:00.740
10x leverage: does the exchange hand you 900 extra? Next episode.

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:03.300
Understand first, then act.
